# tls_engine.c. "fail-closed" lines are valid chains mbedTLS refuses: an availability cost, not
# a security one. "DEVIATION" lines are chains limbo wants refused that mbedTLS accepts.
# limbo.c presents the intermediates in server order (on a path to a trusted certificate; every
# such path is tried), so these lines describe what mbedTLS does with a chain a server sends.
# What it does with a chain out of order is in the x509-misordered section below.
