# ---- X.509 chains out of order (x509-misordered: limbo's own order) ------------------------
# mbedTLS looks for each certificate's parent only among the certificates after it in the
# Certificate message (x509_crt.c:2400, child->next) and does not go back. So a chain whose
# intermediates are not in path order can be refused although a path exists, and a chain
# with alternative issuers can be judged on whichever comes first. In server order (x509-limbo)
# these cases get the outcome recorded there.
