# ---- Security deviations: ESP-IDF's certificate bundle (x509-bundle) ------------------------
# security-deviation <tag>: accepted where it should be refused, by design of the code under
# test, not a bug of this version. Printed on the SECURITY DEVIATIONS line of every run; the run
# fails when one no longer shows, and CRYPTO_STRICT=1 counts them as failures.
# tls_engine.c's TLS_OPEN_CA_BUNDLE mode verifies with esp_crt_bundle_attach() (tls_engine.c:274):
# an empty CA chain and esp_crt_verify_callback(). For a certificate whose flags are
# NOT_TRUSTED, with BAD_MD masked off, the callback looks up the issuer's name in the bundle,
# checks that one signature with the bundle's key and clears every flag
# (esp_crt_bundle.c:84-142 at ESP-IDF c8fc5f64, unchanged in v5.3.6). A bundle entry is a name
# and a key only (gen_crt_bundle.py), so nothing about the root itself is checked. Each chain is
# also run with the root as the CA chain (tc=...::ca), where it is refused.
x509 tc=bundle::sha1-leaf::bundle security-deviation bundle-sha1-below-root BAD_MD is masked off (esp_crt_bundle.c:90): a SHA-1 signature by a bundled root is accepted
x509 tc=bundle::sha1-intermediate::bundle security-deviation bundle-sha1-below-root BAD_MD is masked off (esp_crt_bundle.c:90): a SHA-1 intermediate under a bundled root is accepted
x509 tc=bundle::expired-root::bundle security-deviation bundle-root-validity-unchecked the bundle keeps no validity: an expired root still verifies what it signed
x509 tc=bundle::rsa1024-root::bundle security-deviation bundle-root-key-size-unchecked the callback verifies with the bundle key outside the certificate profile: an RSA-1024 root is accepted
x509 tc=bundle-confused-wide::K0-secp256k1-root::bundle security-deviation bundle-root-curve-unchecked the callback verifies with the bundle key outside the certificate profile: a secp256k1 root, a curve not in mbedTLS's default profile, is accepted
# Not a deviation but its opposite: a server that sends a cross-signed root (the new root's name
# and key, issued by an old root) as its top certificate, with only the new root in the bundle.
# The callback looks up the top certificate's issuer, the old root, and nothing else
# (esp_crt_bundle.c:84-142), so the valid chain is refused. ESP-IDF 6's
# CROSS_SIGNED_VERIFY accepts it (expectations.4).
# The bundle is looked up by the raw bytes of the issuer name (esp_crt_bundle.c:117), where RFC 5280
# 7.1 compares names case-insensitively and across string types (mbedTLS does in CA mode), and
# BAD_MD is masked off for any hash the pk layer can verify, SHA-224 included (esp_crt_bundle.c:90).
x509 tc=bundle-idf6::T2-issuer-case-differs::bundle reject fail-closed: the issuer is looked up by its raw bytes (esp_crt_bundle.c:117), so ROOT A does not find Root A
x509 tc=bundle-idf6::T2b-issuer-printable::bundle reject fail-closed: the issuer is looked up by its raw bytes (esp_crt_bundle.c:117), so a PrintableString Root A does not find the UTF8String one
x509 tc=bundle-idf6::T4-sha224-honest::bundle security-deviation bundle-sha224-below-root BAD_MD is masked off (esp_crt_bundle.c:90): a SHA-224 signature by a bundled root is accepted
x509 tc=cross::top-cross-signed::bundle reject fail-closed: only the top certificate's issuer is looked up in the bundle (esp_crt_bundle.c:84-142), here the old root, which it does not have
